[00:51.17] Well the night that was high, we got into town
[00:56.72] Was the night that the rain, it froze on the ground
[01:02.52] Down the street I heard such a sorrowful tune
[01:07.95] Comin' from the place they call the Spanish Moon
[01:24.29] Well I stepped inside, and stood by the door
[01:30.19] While a dark-eyed girl sang, and played the guitar
[01:35.93] Hookers, and hustlers, filled up the room
[01:41.65] I heard about this place they call the Spanish Moon
[01:47.36] One false step, you get done in
[01:52.74] It's a cold situation
[01:57.94] If that -- that don't -- kill you soon
[02:03.92] The women will down at the Spanish Moon
[02:43.69] I pawned my watch, and I sold my ring
[02:48.76] Just to hear that girl singing, (hear that girl sing)
[02:54.71] Don't take long, to wake up ruined
[03:00.24] The women will down at the Spanish Moon